From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 23:20:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: report extender signal freshness end to end

Associated STA Link Metrics already carry the bSTA RCPI and measurement age, but the controller stored report receipt time. Repeated responses could therefore make an old cached observation look current. Reconstruct the observation timestamp from the standard time-delta field and exercise its rounding behavior.

Expose an explicit fresh, stale, or unknown signal object for each wireless extender edge. Accept timestamped standards RCPI only, including the valid RCPI-zero boundary; do not promote association-time SignalStrength into live telemetry. Keep fresh legacy fields for older API consumers.

Show the state on every wireless backhaul label and hover, refresh telemetry without rebuilding the D3 layout, and preserve compatibility with the existing flat API while its prebuilt helper is refreshed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Its page hunks (src/rdkb-cli/static) moved to easymesh-medium's topology-ui,
which builds the page the controller image serves.
